  "solutions": [
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_075"
      ],
      "explanation": "\\(\\sqrt{a^2}=|a|\\). When \\(a<0\\), \\(|a|=-a\\), so the result is \\(-a\\) (which is positive).",
      "id": "cnm_075_q3_m1",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_075_q3#cnm_075_q3_m1",
      "title": "Use absolute value"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_075"
      ],
      "explanation": "Since \\(a<0\\), the number \\(-a\\) is positive and satisfies \\((-a)^2=a^2\\). The principal square root is the nonnegative square root, so \\(\\sqrt{a^2}=-a\\), choice A.",
      "id": "cnm_075_q3_m2",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_075_q3#cnm_075_q3_m2",
      "title": "Use the principal-root definition"
